      "role": "user",
      "content": "Interesting. I noticed you're leaning quite heavily into certain aesthetics for these groups. For example, you mentioned \"luxurious\" for the UAE and \"vibrant/bold\" for Nigeria, but for Hiroshi you suggested \"minimalistic/monochrome\" and for Liam you suggested \"natural/earthy.\"\n\nAre these suggestions based on actual user data regarding their financial sophistication, or is it more about how we can use these cultural \"looks\" to make them feel more at home? I want to make sure we aren't pigeonholing them. Like, would a \"vibrant\" UI for the Nigerian segment actually suggest a more casual or less serious financial tool compared to a \"minimalist\" one for Japan? Walk me through the logic behind these specific aesthetic choices for each.",
